-- title:
--   Inertia field is unramified; all ramification lies above it
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ and $M$ be number fields with $M$ an $F$-algebra such that $M/F$ is Galois, let $Q$ be a maximal ideal of the ring of integers $\mathcal{O}_M$, and let $E$ be an intermediate field of $M/F$ which is assumed to equal the fixed field in $M$ of the inertia subgroup $Q.\mathrm{inertia}$ of $\mathrm{Gal}(M/F) = M \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[F]} M$, that is, of the subgroup of those $\sigma$ with $\sigma x \equiv x \pmod{Q}$ for every $x \in \mathcal{O}_M$. Write $Q$ under a subring for the contraction of $Q$ along the inclusion of rings of integers, so that $Q \cap \mathcal{O}_F$ and $Q \cap \mathcal{O}_E$ are the primes of $F$ and of $E$ below $Q$. The conclusion is the conjunction of two statements about ramification indices (`Ideal.ramificationIdx'`): first, the ramification index of $Q \cap \mathcal{O}_E$ over $Q \cap \mathcal{O}_F$ equals $1$, so $E/F$ is unramified at this prime; second, the ramification index of $Q$ over $Q \cap \mathcal{O}_E$ equals the ramification index of $Q$ over $Q \cap \mathcal{O}_F$, so all ramification of $Q$ over $F$ takes place in $M/E$.
--
--   This is the classical description of the inertia field of a prime in a Galois extension of number fields: the fixed field of the inertia group is unramified at the prime below it and carries none of the ramification. It is used in the project to show that, for an element of the inertia field, the $Q$-valuation lies in the subgroup generated by the ramification index, in [`ValuationSubring.exists_valuation_mul_zpow_eq_one_of_forall_inertia_apply_eq`](thm.html#ValuationSubring.exists_valuation_mul_zpow_eq_one_of_forall_inertia_apply_eq).
